  "user_request_original": "Design a 24-layer planar dielectric stack on fused silica substrate with air incidence. Layer sequence: HfO2, SiO2 (Lemarchand), HfO2, SiO2 (Lemarchand), HfO2, SiO2 (Lemarchand), HfO2, SiO2 (Lemarchand), HfO2, SiO2 (Lemarchand), HfO2, SiO2 (Lemarchand), HfO2, SiO2 (Lemarchand), HfO2, SiO2 (Lemarchand), HfO2, SiO2 (Lemarchand), HfO2, SiO2 (Lemarchand), HfO2, SiO2 (Lemarchand), HfO2, SiO2 (Lemarchand) (alternating, starting with HfO2, ending with SiO2 (Lemarchand) before substrate). Optimize individual layer thicknesses using gradient-based optimization. Initialize thicknesses from quarter-wave optical thickness centers calculated at 550 nm (reflection band center) and 1547 nm (transmission band center) with Gaussian variance of ±25% around QWOT values. Apply coupling penalty during optimization enforcing n_H*d_H ≈ n_L*d_L for adjacent HfO2/SiO2 (Lemarchand) pairs. Wavelength bands: 400-700 nm (maximize reflectance), 1530-1565 nm (maximize transmittance). Normal incidence (0 degrees). Total layer count fixed at 24. Materials: hfo2 and SiO2 (Lemarchand) from material catalog.",
